{
  /*
   * The generator's type check (`npm run compile`, run by the Terraform
   * Provider Generation workflow) and jest's (ts-jest compiles with this
   * file).
   *
   * The generator imports Common's sources: Core/ResourceGenerator.ts and
   * GenerateProvider.ts through the "Common/*" alias, and GenerateProvider.ts
   * imports ../OpenAPI/GenerateSpec.ts, which reaches Common's whole server
   * (every model). A program has one set of compiler options for every file
   * in it, so those files are checked with the options written here. Common's
   * models are written for Common's options - experimentalDecorators,
   * strictNullChecks - and this file used to have its own (strict: false, no
   * decorators): about 10,700 errors in Common files that pass `npx tsc` in
   * packages/Common.
   *
   * So it extends Common's tsconfig. Common's files are checked exactly as
   * packages/Common checks them (strictness, target, lib, decorators, jsx,
   * and the "Common/*" alias, which Common's file resolves to
   * packages/Common), and the generator's own files - Core/, Tests/ and
   * GenerateProvider.ts - are held to the same strict rules, as they already
   * are wherever else they are compiled: Common's test type-check imports
   * Core/ (packages/Common/Tests), and `npm run generate-terraform-provider`
   * runs them through ts-node with the repository root's strict tsconfig.
   *
   * Only what has to differ is set here:
   *   - module: jest and ts-node run these files as CommonJS. Common's own
   *     "es2022" is for its build; it checks the same imports.
   *   - noEmit: this is a check. Nothing is built from it.
   *   - typeRoots and types: the generator's own @types - jest 30 for its
   *     jest 30 tests - instead of Common's. Its @types/node is the version
   *     Common's is, so Node's APIs read the same in both programs.
   *   - include: the generator's files, and Common's global declarations
   *     (ambient modules such as "*.png"), which Common's own compile sees
   *     through its default include; a Common file that relies on one would
   *     otherwise fail here only.
   *
   * Tests/TypeCheckConfig.test.ts pins all of this.
   */
  "extends": "../../packages/Common/tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "module": "commonjs",
    "noEmit": true,
    "typeRoots": ["./node_modules/@types"],
    "types": ["node", "jest"]
  },
  "include": [
    "Core/**/*.ts",
    "Tests/**/*.ts",
    "GenerateProvider.ts",
    "../../packages/Common/Typings/**/*.d.ts",
    "../../packages/Common/UI/index.d.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": ["node_modules"]
}
